<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-cervera-levin-mafe-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Code-to-model traceability: 68/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "At commit 5659d5e (following commit 0154143), model constants are centralized, f2_for_shift() properly inverts wavefront_for_f2() without clipping, and Panel D dynamically formats pulse bounds (1.0-16.0 h) and posterior head-readout percentages (91.8% vs 23.5%) from simulation state. Deducts 32 points because the 1D RD equations and the pharynx-posterior phenotype threshold (x*_b = 0.5833, which includes 20-unit plotting padding and a 100-unit cartoon pharynx convention) do not map to published equations in Cervera et al. (2021). Evidence: 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L320–L359: pharynx-boundary criterion and unclipped f2_for_shift() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L320-L359>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1271–L1318: Panel D dynamic pulse span and readout percentage labels <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1271-L1318>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 6.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-cervera-levin-mafe-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Model fidelity to source: 50/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Explicitly documents in its header scope statement that the full texts of Cervera, Levin & Mafe (2021) and Cervera et al. (2020) were not accessible and that the 1D reaction-diffusion solver (rd_antagonistic_1d and rd_linear_1d) and rusty-matter 2-node ODE port are qualitative analogues. At commit 5659d5e, f2 and f3 both drive distinct 1D boundary-value solvers, and the inverse threshold finder f2_for_shift() bisects on the unclipped wavefront x*(f2) = x*_b (recovering f2_b = 0.422 where x*(f2_b) = 0.5833). Held at 50 because the equations and constants are local constructions rather than verified transcriptions of the 2021/2020 papers, rd_antagonistic_1d's docstring (line 231) still claims to implement the paper's equations, and m3 (f3) is not coupled to any morphological boundary. Evidence: 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L27–L47: explicit scope statement disclaiming equation-level fidelity to the inaccessible 2021/2020 full papers <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L27-L47>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L213–L359: rd_antagonistic_1d(), rd_linear_1d(), wavefront_for_f2(), and unclipped f2_for_shift() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L213-L359>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-cervera-levin-mafe-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Morphometric validation: 54/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Fits a 1-parameter linear mapping f2(p) = 1 - a*p to Oviedo et al. (2010) octanol double-head frequencies across 4 axial crop positions (training RMSE = 4.19 percentage points) and evaluates it without refitting on held-out triple-innexin RNAi crops (test RMSE = 23.52 percentage points, r = 0.943), while verifying rusty-matter trace parity across all 5 scenarios (max |delta| = 0.0332) and computing Planform #1 vs #2 silhouette IoU (0.9478). Held at 54 because the 4-point empirical sample is tiny, the 23.5-point held-out error is large, and no morphometric dimensions of real regenerated double-head specimens are measured. Evidence: 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L997–L1026: 1-parameter octanol training fit and held-out RNAi evaluation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L997-L1026>; cervera_levin_mafe_metrics.csv L1–L55: exported wavefront, silhouette-area, and empirical fit metrics <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/cervera_levin_mafe_metrics.csv#L1-L55>. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): rusty-matter trace parity, max |Δ| = 0.0332 state units (reference 0.0, MesmerPrism/rusty-matter commit ad111fa7ecfd8f43d292ff3b1d27d3af2741d828) [maximum absolute difference across all 5 scenarios, 11 sampled steps and 4 state averages against rusty_matter_planarian_traces.json]; symmetric RD wavefront x*(f2=1) = 0.5 AP fraction (reference 0.5, symmetric boundary conditions at x=0 and x=L) [zero crossing of m1(x) - m2(x) when D2 = D2_0]; pharynx-boundary criterion x*_b = 0.5833 AP fraction [posterior end of the Planform #1 wild-type pharynx on the AP extent] — crossed at f2_b = 0.4197 (where x*(f2_b) = 0.5833); anterior body-area fraction on S. mediterranea silhouette (f2=1 -> f2=0.25) = 0.1561 fraction of body area [increase in real-silhouette mask area anterior to x*(f2) from f2=1.0 (0.483) to f2=0.25 (0.639)]; ML centre/edge ratio λ(f3), f3=1.0 vs f3=0.3 = 0.1855 ratio difference (reference >0 (monotonic decrease under lateral gap-junction blockade)) [m3(L_z/2)/m3(0) drop from f3=1.0 (0.197) to f3=0.3 (0.011)]; Oviedo 2010 octanol crop-gradient training RMSE = 4.1871 percentage points (reference 0.0, PlanformDB 2.5.0 / Oviedo et al. 2010 Dev. Biol. 339:188) [1-parameter fit f2(p) = 1 - 0.58*p against Oviedo et al. 2010 octanol double-head frequencies (Exps 415-418, n=4 crops)]; Oviedo 2010 triple-innexin RNAi held-out RMSE = 23.5215 percentage points (reference 0.0, PlanformDB 2.5.0 / Oviedo et al. 2010 Dev. Biol. 339:188) [held-out prediction error of the octanol-fitted curve against Dj-Inx-12 + Dj-Inx-5/13 RNAi double-head frequencies (Exps 446-449, n=4 crops)] — Pearson r = 0.943; circuit posterior head readout, memory ON vs memory OFF control = 0.9185 readout [0,1] (reference 0.23491399812436778, TransientDepolarizationNoMemoryControl negative control (Durant et al. 2019 Biophys. J. 116:948)) [final posterior head-identity readout R_head,post under TransientDepolarizationMemory] — hysteresis memory sustains depolarised head fate after transient pulse ends; Planform #1 Wild Type vs #2 Double Head silhouette IoU = 0.9478 ratio (reference <1.0 (posterior tail replaced by ectopic head cap), PlanformDB 2.5.0 morphologies #1 and #2) [256x256 shared-canvas intersection-over-union of decoded Lobo et al. (2013) graph silhouettes]." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasProbability 5.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-cervera-levin-mafe-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — MorphoEval overall 60.7/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Blinded second-assessor pass (gemini-4-argon) at commit 5659d5e (including the commit 0154143 fixes for f2_for_shift() and Panel D legend strings). Combines a local 1D reaction-diffusion analogue (AP m1/m2 + orthogonal ML m3), a deterministic Python port of the rusty-matter 2-node bioelectric circuit, a 1-parameter crop-position fit to Oviedo et al. (2010) octanol data tested on held-out innexin-RNAi data, and morphogen territory projection onto a segmented S. mediterranea photograph alongside two decoded Planform cartoons. Overall 60.7/100 (faithfulness 51.9, reproducibility 81.3; model-implementation 54.0/100, biological-validation 50.2/100, applicable-only overall 60.7/100; uncalibrated rubric score, not a calibrated probability); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 5659d5e; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, pandas 2.3.3, scikit-image 0.26.0, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 50, Morphological realism / specimen match 48, Parameter expressivity 62, Morphometric validation 54, Source and data traceability 84, Code-to-model traceability 68, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: cervera_levin_mafe_gj_block.gif: rendered output of 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py at 5659d5e, image/gif, 1398777 B, 560×378 px, 46 frames, sha256 214238f0d75fdcfa702b96ce3fcb12fcafe48ed08e52c26bbcbfc1faf6bab427." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe> ;
    pk:hasProbability 6.07e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-cervera-levin-mafe-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Parameter expressivity: 62/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Sweeps f2 across [0.25, 1.0] (monotonically shifting the AP wavefront x*(f2) from 0.500 to 0.648 and anterior silhouette area from 0.483 to 0.639) and sweeps f3 across [0.30, 1.0] (reducing the ML centre/edge ratio lambda(f3) from 0.197 to 0.011), and compares 5 rusty-matter bioelectric scenarios across 3 crop positions. Deducts 38 points because f3 has no effect on the rendered 2D worm morphology and the phenotype output is a binary switch rather than a continuous morphogenetic deformation. Evidence: 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L302–L359: wavefront_for_f2(), lateral_index_for_f3(), and f2_for_shift() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L302-L359>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L965–L978: f2 and f3 parameter sweeps <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L965-L978>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 6.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-cervera-levin-mafe-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Reproducibility package: 88/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Fully deterministic solver and rendering pipeline, SHA-256 input verification, comprehensive --self-test gate (which now asserts exact inverse recovery of f2_b as well as symmetry, monotonicity, f3 sensitivity, and trace parity), headless CLI flags, and pinned dependencies in requirements.lock.txt. Evidence: 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1412–L1456: self_test_model() including f2_b inverse-recovery assertion <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1412-L1456>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1545–L1605: CLI argument parser and exit-code handling <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1545-L1605>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-repro-package> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-cervera-levin-mafe-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Source and data traceability: 84/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Cites DOIs and corrected PMIDs for Cervera et al. (2020, 2021), Oviedo et al. (2010), Durant et al. (2019), and Lobo et al. (2013), pins all three vendored JSON fixtures and the Wikimedia Commons photograph by SHA-256, and transparently documents which papers were consulted only via abstract/presentation. Evidence: 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L6–L47: bibliographic citations and source-access disclosure <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L6-L47>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L98–L130: SHA-256 pins for fixtures and Smediterranea.jpg <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L98-L130>." ;
