<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-cervera-levin-mafe-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Morphological realism / specimen match: 48/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Segments a real Wikimedia Commons photograph of Schmidtea mediterranea (Stevenson & Beane 2010, SHA-256 verified) to measure the body-area fraction anterior to x*(f2) and renders decoded Planform #1 Wild Type and #2 Double Head cartoons. Held below 50 because the 1D signals are merely painted onto a static wild-type photograph whose outline never deforms into a double-headed worm, and the morphology readout switches categorically between two pre-drawn Planform cartoons at an assumed pharynx-posterior threshold x*_b = 0.5833. Evidence: 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L150–L207: load_real_planarian_silhouette() segments a static wild-type S. mediterranea mask <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L150-L207>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L795–L869: static Planform #1 and #2 cartoon templates <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L795-L869>; cervera_levin_mafe_bioelectric_morphospace.png (generated output, not in repo): 6-panel summary figure — cervera_levin_mafe_bioelectric_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py at 5659d5e, image/png, 547708 B, 2330×1781 px, sha256 3f521835636f3530ddf73b0ea3142db13d605b319aac93fc940e3d8f07fc5f77." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasProbability 4.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-chindapol-coral-flow-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Chindapol flow-driven coral growth — Code-to-model traceability: 68/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Both the header docstring and Figure panel (f) ('From the paper to this demo') explicitly map each concept in Chindapol et al. (2013) to its 2D DLA counterpart, though individual functions do not cite specific equation numbers from the paper's Methods. Evidence: 2013-chindapol-coral-flow.py L11–L36: docstring mapping paper concepts to demo approximations <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2013-chindapol-coral-flow.py#L11-L36>; 2013-chindapol-coral-flow.py L252–L273: Panel (f) correspondence table <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2013-chindapol-coral-flow.py#L252-L273>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-chindapol-coral-flow-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 6.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-chindapol-coral-flow-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Chindapol flow-driven coral growth — Model fidelity to source: 38/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Honestly declares in the module docstring and in Panel (f) that the paper's coupled 3D laminar Navier-Stokes flow solver, nutrient advection-diffusion boundary layer, and normal-flux surface extension law are replaced by a 2D square-lattice biased random walk (DLA with drift + basal nutrient-shadowing survival probability). While the substitution is transparent, a stochastic particle-sticking walk on a 2D grid is a fundamentally different physical mechanism from continuum hydrodynamic advection-diffusion around a 3D branching colony, and the Peclet number Pe = u_0*L/D is not computed. Evidence: 2013-chindapol-coral-flow.py L11–L36: docstring explicitly states 3D Navier-Stokes/COMSOL is replaced by 2D DLA-with-drift <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2013-chindapol-coral-flow.py#L11-L36>; 2013-chindapol-coral-flow.py L65–L137: simulate_coral() 2D lattice random walk with drift bias <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2013-chindapol-coral-flow.py#L65-L137>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-chindapol-coral-flow-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 3.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-chindapol-coral-flow-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Chindapol flow-driven coral growth — Morphometric validation: 48/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Computes 2D analogues of the paper's angular branch-tip orientation metrics (hangle = atan2(dx, dy), smmag = |mean(sign(hangle))|, and circular resultant length Rbar) on local distance-transform maxima in morphometrics(). Held below 50 because tip detection operates on noisy 2D lattice pixels rather than 3D skeletal medial axes, and no numerical values from Chindapol et al. (2013) Figs. 9-12 or CT-scanned coral colonies are compared. Evidence: 2013-chindapol-coral-flow.py L150–L179: branch_tips() and morphometrics() computing hangle, smmag, and Rbar <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2013-chindapol-coral-flow.py#L150-L179>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-chindapol-coral-flow-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasProbability 4.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-chindapol-coral-flow-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Chindapol flow-driven coral growth — MorphoEval overall 56.0/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Blinded second-assessor pass (gemini-4-argon). Replaces Chindapol et al.'s (2013) 3D COMSOL Navier-Stokes + advection-diffusion accretive growth model of Pocillopora verrucosa with a declared 2D lattice diffusion-limited aggregation (DLA) random walk with horizontal drift, reproducing qualitative upstream-bending and compactification trends across five drift values. Overall 56.0/100 (faithfulness 46.4, reproducibility 78.3; model-implementation 49.3/100, biological-validation 44.2/100, applicable-only overall 56.0/100; uncalibrated rubric score, not a calibrated probability); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 5659d5e; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, pandas 2.3.3, scikit-image 0.26.0, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 38, Morphological realism / specimen match 42, Parameter expressivity 72, Morphometric validation 48, Source and data traceability 82, Code-to-model traceability 68, Reproducibility package 82. Output judged: chindapol_coral_flow_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2013-chindapol-coral-flow.py at 5659d5e, image/png, 235376 B, 1726×1231 px, sha256 c431f9a5ae368f84965ccd6e8762c61c5db8f77323de69daab92a26de99e1626." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-chindapol-coral-flow> ;
    pk:hasProbability 5.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

