<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-chindapol-coral-flow-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Chindapol flow-driven coral growth — Morphological realism / specimen match: 42/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Renders five 2D dendritic lattice clusters (700 particles each) that transition from radially symmetric branching at drift=0.00 to upstream-skewed, compactified forms at drift=0.22. However, the 1-pixel-wide jagged 2D DLA trees lack the smooth, thick, club-shaped 3D branches of Pocillopora verrucosa and no CT scans or figures from Chindapol et al. (2013) are overlaid. Evidence: 2013-chindapol-coral-flow.py L186–L231: five drift regimes rendered in panels (a)-(c) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2013-chindapol-coral-flow.py#L186-L231>; docs/media/chindapol_coral_flow_growth.gif (generated output, not in repo): animated 2D DLA growth across three flow regimes — docs/media/chindapol_coral_flow_growth.gif: rendered output of 2013-chindapol-coral-flow.py at 5659d5e, image/gif, 737329 B, 720×288 px, 48 frames, sha256 30eaa02efc49579c08d71254de928be3a6e626a25e19cea1b4b36b39478e3442." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-chindapol-coral-flow-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasProbability 4.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Odonata wing cells through deep time — Code-to-model traceability: 88/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Clear modular pipeline separating archive verification (_fetch), PBDB age lookup (pbdb_ages, AGE_OVERRIDES), raster scale-bar parsing (_read_drawing), morphological segmentation (segment_fossil_cells), convex-hull Feret caliper measurement (_max_feret), and figure generation. Evidence: 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L149–L224: AGE_OVERRIDES and pbdb_ages() with documented stratigraphic stage midpoints <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L149-L224>; 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L305–L419: documented 4-step segmentation and Feret diameter pipeline <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L305-L419>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Odonata wing cells through deep time — Model fidelity to source: 88/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Operationalises the scaling prediction of Hoffmann et al. (2018) (a fixed developmental inhibition radius r_in yields N ~ L^2 and median cell length ~ L^0) via log-log OLS regressions (ols_loglog) and replicates Eshghi et al.'s (2026) morphometric pipeline from raw fossil TIFFs by reading embedded scale bars, skeletonising veins, labelling connected interior regions, and measuring cell area, perimeter, circularity, and exact convex-hull maximum Feret diameter (_max_feret). Deducts 12 points because fossil_drawing() (used for rendering outlines, threshold < 128, largest connected component) and _read_drawing() (used for cell segmentation, threshold < 160, all wing components >= 150 px) use slightly different binarisation/component rules, and the statistical test is an observational scaling analysis rather than a mechanistic simulation. Evidence: 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L137–L143: ols_loglog() fits log10(y) = a + b*log10(x) against theoretical slopes b=2 and b=0 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L137-L143>; 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L352–L419: segment_fossil_cells(), _max_feret(), and cell_table() re-derive cell counts and Feret diameters <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L352-L419>; 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L255–L349: threshold and component-filtering difference between fossil_drawing() (<128) and _read_drawing() (<160) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L255-L349>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Odonata wing cells through deep time — Morphometric validation: 96/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Quantifies scaling slopes, R^2, p-values, and median/IQR cell lengths across fossil and extant suborders (N ~ L^1.78, R^2 = 0.87 for fossils; N ~ L^1.45, R^2 = 0.65 for extant; median cell length 0.78-0.99 mm across 150 Myr and a 6x wing-length range) and validates per-cell morphometrics (count, median, mean, IQR, 95th percentile Feret diameter, area, circularity) across all 69 fossil wings in datasets/odonata/fossil_wing_resegmentation.csv. Evidence: 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L613–L667: build_static_figure() computes and annotates log-log OLS slopes, R^2, and suborder medians/IQRs <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L613-L667>; 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L689–L732: build_resegmentation_figure() plots cell-count and median-length parity scatters <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L689-L732>; datasets/odonata/fossil_wing_resegmentation.csv L1–L70: exported per-wing validation metrics <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/datasets/odonata/fossil_wing_resegmentation.csv#L1-L70>. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): cell count ∝ wing length^b, fossil = 1.7811 exponent (reference 2.0, isometric prediction for a constant cell size (Hoffmann et al. 2018 inhibition length)) [OLS slope of log10 cell count on log10 wing length, n=69 wings (Eshghi et al. 2026 tables)] — r = 0.739; median cell length ∝ wing length^b, fossil = -0.1673 exponent (reference 0.0, constant cell size) [OLS slope of log10 median cell length on log10 wing length]; median cell length over wings, fossil = 0.7837 mm [median over wings of the per-wing median cell length (Eshghi et al. 2026 tables)] — IQR 0.67–0.94 mm; cell count ∝ wing length^b, extant_dragonfly = 1.111 exponent (reference 2.0, isometric prediction for a constant cell size (Hoffmann et al. 2018 inhibition length)) [OLS slope of log10 cell count on log10 wing length, n=290 wings (Eshghi et al. 2026 tables)] — r = 0.816; median cell length ∝ wing length^b, extant_dragonfly = 0.2171 exponent (reference 0.0, constant cell size) [OLS slope of log10 median cell length on log10 wing length]; median cell length over wings, extant_dragonfly = 0.9885 mm [median over wings of the per-wing median cell length (Eshghi et al. 2026 tables)] — IQR 0.87–1.09 mm; cell count ∝ wing length^b, extant_damselfly = 1.0078 exponent (reference 2.0, isometric prediction for a constant cell size (Hoffmann et al. 2018 inhibition length)) [OLS slope of log10 cell count on log10 wing length, n=104 wings (Eshghi et al. 2026 tables)] — r = 0.872; median cell length ∝ wing length^b, extant_damselfly = 0.2765 exponent (reference 0.0, constant cell size) [OLS slope of log10 median cell length on log10 wing length]; median cell length over wings, extant_damselfly = 0.8991 mm [median over wings of the per-wing median cell length (Eshghi et al. 2026 tables)] — IQR 0.83–0.99 mm; fossil drawings re-segmented = 69 count (reference 69, fossil wings in Table S1) [fossil venation drawings in the Zenodo archive segmented by the script]; scale bar label read from the drawing = 65 count (reference 69) [drawings whose scale-bar label was read from the glyphs and found consistent with the tabulated wing length] — the rest use the bar with a value inferred from the tabulated wing length, or that length alone; cell count, median |ΔN|/N vs Table S1 = 0.0 ratio (reference 0.0, Eshghi et al. 2026 Table S1) [per-wing relative difference between the script's cell count and the published count, median over 69 wings] — 90% of wings within 2%; max 194% (#7, drawing and table row disagree); median cell length, median |Δ| vs Table S1 = 0.0339 ratio (reference 0.0, Eshghi et al. 2026 Table S1) [per-wing relative difference of the median cell length (maximum Feret diameter), median over wings] — signed mean +3.5% (cells bounded by vein mid-lines); largest cell length, median |Δ| vs Table S1 = 0.0094 ratio (reference 0.0, Eshghi et al. 2026 Table S1) [as above for the largest cell of each wing]; fossil median cell length, re-segmented = 0.8275 mm (reference 0.7837, same statistic from Table S1) [median over wings of the script's own per-wing median cell length]." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasProbability 9.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Odonata wing cells through deep time — MorphoEval overall 87.3/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Blinded second-assessor pass (gemini-4-argon). Tests the macroevolutionary prediction of Hoffmann et al.'s (2018) inhibition-zone venation model (conserved inhibition length -> cell count N ~ L^2 and cell length ~ L^0) across 69 Mesozoic-Cenozoic fossil wings and 394 extant Odonata wings from Eshghi et al. (2026), and independently re-segments the 69 fossil wing line drawings from pixel scale bars to verify Table S1. Overall 87.3/100 (faithfulness 85.7, reproducibility 91.1; model-implementation 75.3/100, biological-validation 93.5/100, applicable-only overall 91.5/100; uncalibrated rubric score, not a calibrated probability); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 5659d5e; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, pandas 2.3.3, scikit-image 0.26.0, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 92, Parameter expressivity 50, Morphometric validation 96, Source and data traceability 95, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: odonata_fossil_resegmentation.png: rendered output of 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py at 5659d5e, image/png, 286190 B, 1663×1323 px, sha256 ab6f3b9f89fbcff0ff1fa942915cfcb3736ebde60723489a9ee8d7a39c8a5b38." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.73e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Odonata wing cells through deep time — Parameter expressivity: 50/100" ;
