<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Odonata wing cells through deep time — Reproducibility package: 90/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Fully deterministic pipeline (no stochastic steps), SHA-256-verified auto-download and local caching (.odonata_cache/), vendored summary tables in datasets/odonata/, and pinned environment in requirements.txt / requirements.lock.txt. Deducts 10 points because running the script requires downloading ~95 MB of external archives on a cold cache and overwrites the tracked file datasets/odonata/fossil_wing_resegmentation.csv in place without CLI flags. Evidence: 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L75–L86: _fetch() automatic download and SHA-256 digest check <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L75-L86>; 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L447–L452: resegment_all_fossils() writes directly to tracked CSV path <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L447-L452>; requirements.lock.txt L1–L35: pinned dependency lockfile <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/requirements.lock.txt#L1-L35>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-repro-package> ;
    pk:hasProbability 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Odonata wing cells through deep time — Source and data traceability: 95/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Cites Eshghi et al. (2026) Zenodo archive (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.19899648), Hoffmann et al. (2018) PNAS (DOI 10.1073/pnas.1721248115), and the Paleobiology Database Odonatoptera query URL; verifies SHA-256 digests of both remote archives (ESH_ZIP_SHA256 and HOFF_TAR_SHA256) in _fetch() and documents every vendored CSV in datasets/odonata/README.md. Evidence: 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L66–L86: ESH_ZIP_URL, ESH_ZIP_SHA256, HOFF_TAR_URL, and HOFF_TAR_SHA256 with _fetch() verification <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L66-L86>; datasets/odonata/README.md L1–L108: dataset provenance, PBDB age resolution rules, and source anomaly documentation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/datasets/odonata/README.md#L1-L108>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-source-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 9.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Odonata wing cells through deep time — Morphological realism / specimen match: 92/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Renders real fossil wing line drawings from Eshghi et al. (2026) at true millimetre scale colour-coded by per-cell Feret diameter alongside extant segmented wings from Hoffmann et al. (2018) (Arigomphus villosipes and Aeshna cyanea). Across the 67 non-swapped fossil wings, the independent re-segmentation matches Table S1 cell counts to a median signed difference of 0.0% (IQR -0.6% to +0.2%; 60/67 within 2%) and median cell length to +3.4%, while identifying two concrete curatorial errors in the published table (15_Cymatophlebia_longialata and the swapped 58/59 pair). Evidence: 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L422–L464: resegment_all_fossils() and KNOWN_SOURCE_DISCREPANCIES <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L422-L464>; datasets/odonata/fossil_wing_resegmentation.csv L1–L70: 69-wing comparison of Table S1 vs independent re-segmentation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/datasets/odonata/fossil_wing_resegmentation.csv#L1-L70>; odonata_fossil_resegmentation.png (generated output, not in repo): four fossil wings rendered at common mm scale alongside parity scatters against Table S1 — odonata_fossil_resegmentation.png: rendered output of 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py at 5659d5e, image/png, 286190 B, 1663×1323 px, sha256 ab6f3b9f89fbcff0ff1fa942915cfcb3736ebde60723489a9ee8d7a39c8a5b38." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasProbability 9.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-hoffmann-wing-venation-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hoffmann-Donoughe insect wing venation — Code-to-model traceability: 78/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Module docstring clearly maps the 5-step pipeline to SI sections 3.3-3.4 and explains where the implementation simplifies the paper's thickness-based density estimate, though individual helper functions do not cite equation or figure numbers. Evidence: 2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py L12–L34: 5-step correspondence to SI 3.3-3.4 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py#L12-L34>; 2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py L164–L195: model_wing() inline comments <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py#L164-L195>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-hoffmann-wing-venation-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-hoffmann-wing-venation-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hoffmann-Donoughe insect wing venation — Model fidelity to source: 82/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Implements the core SI 3.3-3.4 pipeline on the real wing boundary and primary-vein scaffold: local density weighting proportional to 1/cell^2, damped Lloyd equilibration (step 0.55) inside the primary-vein compartments, and secondary veins drawn as Voronoi bisectors between sites sharing the same primary compartment. Deducts 18 points because local cell size is derived from the Euclidean distance transform of the real wing's all-vein mask (dt) rather than from primary-vein thickness as in the paper, and Lloyd relaxation terminates after a fixed n_iter=18 iterations rather than the paper's 0.1%-of-wing-length displacement threshold. Evidence: 2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py L111–L133: segment_wing() derives local cell size from distance_transform_edt(~vein) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py#L111-L133>; 2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py L164–L195: model_wing() seeds n_cells weighted by 1/cell^2 and runs n_iter=18 fixed Lloyd iterations <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py#L164-L195>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-hoffmann-wing-venation-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-hoffmann-wing-venation-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hoffmann-Donoughe insect wing venation — Morphometric validation: 84/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Computes domain circularity c = 4*pi*A/P^2 (using Crofton perimeter), normalised cell area, and proximal-distal circularity profiles across all 923 real and model vein domains and benchmarks both against the regular-hexagon theoretical ceiling pi*sqrt(3)/6 = 0.9069. Deducts 16 points because internal polygon vertex angles and edge-count distributions (pentagons/hexagons/heptagons) analyzed in Hoffmann et al. (2018) are not computed. Evidence: 2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py L69–L69: HEXAGON_CIRC = pi*sqrt(3)/6 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py#L69-L69>; 2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py L200–L214: domain_stats() computes Crofton circularity, area, and x-centroid <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py#L200-L214>; 2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py L298–L334: panels (c)-(e) compare circularity distributions, area vs circularity, and proximal-distal trends <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py#L298-L334>. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): mean domain circularity, model wing = 0.867 ratio (4πA/P²) (reference 0.712, same statistic on the authors' segmented real wing (Hoffmann et al. 2018 example)) [script's domain_stats() over Voronoi domains after Lloyd equilibration (seed 0)] — regular hexagon = 0.907; model n=923, real n=923; vein-domain count, model wing = 923 count (reference 923, same count on the real wing) [domains large enough to measure, model] — equal by construction: the model is seeded with the real wing's domain count; vein-domain count, real wing (all) = 923 count [peaks of the distance transform inside the segmented real wing] — wing area 1905316 px." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-hoffmann-wing-venation-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-hoffmann-wing-venation-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hoffmann-Donoughe insect wing venation — MorphoEval overall 81.3/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Blinded second-assessor pass (gemini-4-argon). Implements Hoffmann et al.'s (2018) SI 3.3-3.4 secondary-vein model (density-weighted seeding, damped centroidal-Voronoi / Lloyd equilibration, and Voronoi bisectors) on the segmented primary-vein scaffold of Arigomphus villosipes (923 vein domains), comparing circularity, area, and proximal-distal trends against the real wing and the regular-hexagon ceiling. Overall 81.3/100 (faithfulness 81.5, reproducibility 80.8; model-implementation 77.3/100, biological-validation 84.6/100, applicable-only overall 81.3/100; uncalibrated rubric score, not a calibrated probability); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 5659d5e; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, pandas 2.3.3, scikit-image 0.26.0, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 82, Morphological realism / specimen match 85, Parameter expressivity 68, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 84, Code-to-model traceability 78, Reproducibility package 80. Output judged: hoffmann_wing_recapitulation.png: rendered output of 2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py at 5659d5e, image/png, 179027 B, 1730×1206 px, sha256 43b99ec8ae8205b3f12cfd0cde6d3ab1935463e222f66a0f5c16ec15d49e1108." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-hoffmann-wing-venation> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.13e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-hoffmann-wing-venation-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hoffmann-Donoughe insect wing venation — Parameter expressivity: 68/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Exposes n_iter, seed, and downsample parameters and animates the full iteration-by-iteration equilibration trajectory (iterations 0..18) along with a live circularity trajectory in make_gif() (docs/media/hoffmann_wing_lloyd.gif), though the static figure make_figure() plots only the final n_iter=18 state and does not vary inhibition-density scaling parameters. Evidence: 2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py L271–L271: make_figure() evaluates only n_iter=18 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py#L271-L271>; 2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py L346–L380: make_gif() animates iterations 0..18 and plots mean circularity vs iteration <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py#L346-L380>; docs/media/hoffmann_wing_lloyd.gif (generated output, not in repo): animated Lloyd equilibration trajectory — docs/media/hoffmann_wing_lloyd.gif: rendered output of 2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py at 5659d5e, image/gif, 901133 B, 720×403 px, 19 frames, sha256 e53e2133c7bebee17e6ac3cab339c9931048bc2f38559d19ab3c98f90ca8260c." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-hoffmann-wing-venation-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 6.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-hoffmann-wing-venation-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hoffmann-Donoughe insect wing venation — Reproducibility package: 80/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Deterministic RNG seeding (np.random.default_rng(seed) with seed=0), CLI flags (--output, --downsample, --gif, --no-show), automatic caching in .wing_cache/, and pinned dependencies (including scikit-image and Pillow) in requirements.txt and requirements.lock.txt. Deducts 20 points because fetch_wing_png() lacks a SHA-256 check on the remote archive and the module docstring on lines 39-40 still states that scikit-image and Pillow are not in requirements.txt. Evidence: 2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py L39–L40: stale docstring note on scikit-image/Pillow <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py#L39-L40>; 2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py L383–L399: CLI argument parser <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py#L383-L399>; requirements.lock.txt L1–L35: pinned dependency lockfile <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/requirements.lock.txt#L1-L35>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-hoffmann-wing-venation-repro-package> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-hoffmann-wing-venation-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hoffmann-Donoughe insect wing venation — Source and data traceability: 84/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Cites Hoffmann et al. (2018) with DOI (10.1073/pnas.1721248115), PMID (30224459), and GitHub repository URL, and fetches the official example wing Arigomphus_villosipes_LHW.png from PNAS_Paper_Code.zip. Deducts 16 points because fetch_wing_png() does not verify a pinned SHA-256 digest on the downloaded ZIP archive or extracted PNG. Evidence: 2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py L5–L10: citation block with DOI, PMID, and GitHub URL <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py#L5-L10>; 2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py L65–L88: ZIP_URL and fetch_wing_png() without SHA-256 verification <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py#L65-L88>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-hoffmann-wing-venation-source-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-hoffmann-wing-venation-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hoffmann-Donoughe insect wing venation — Morphological realism / specimen match: 85/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Places the segmented real Arigomphus villosipes hindwing (panel a) directly beside the model-regenerated secondary venation on the same outline and primary scaffold (panel b), reproducing domain count (923) and proximal-to-distal cell-size gradients. Deducts 15 points because model domains are noticeably more isotropic/hexagonal than the elongated rectangular cell rows between parallel longitudinal veins in the real wing (mean circularity 0.867 vs 0.712). Evidence: 2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py L255–L297: make_figure() renders side-by-side real vs model wings colored by domain circularity <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py#L255-L297>; hoffmann_wing_recapitulation.png (generated output, not in repo): panels (a) and (b) side-by-side specimen vs model comparison — hoffmann_wing_recapitulation.png: rendered output of 2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py at 5659d5e, image/png, 179027 B, 1730×1206 px, sha256 43b99ec8ae8205b3f12cfd0cde6d3ab1935463e222f66a0f5c16ec15d49e1108." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-hoffmann-wing-venation-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-lobo-limbform-morphology-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "LimbformDB limb morphologies — Code-to-model traceability: 86/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Cleanly maps SQLite tables (Morphology, Link, JointParam, LinkSubJoint, Digit) to Python dataclasses and geometric primitives, with detailed ASCII diagrams and docstrings explaining the cyclic bisector rule and sub-joint double-counting convention. Evidence: 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L26–L49: header documentation mapping SQLite tables to geometric decoding rules <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L26-L49>; 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L305–L355: _edges_of() and control_points() with inline geometric comments <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L305-L355>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-lobo-limbform-morphology-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-lobo-limbform-morphology-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "LimbformDB limb morphologies — Model fidelity to source: 88/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Faithfully decodes LimbformDB 2.1.0's five-table relational graph (Morphology, Link, JointParam, LinkSubJoint, Digit) using recursive vector accumulation, cyclic half-angle bisectors at branching joints, +90/+180/+270 deg terminal caps, double-counted host segments at ectopic sub-joints, and periodic Catmull-Rom splines, satisfying the joint-radius count rule on 3,137 of 3,146 joints (99.71%). Deducts 12 points because Link.side, Link.reversed, Link.inverted, and Digit.reversed are parsed into dataclasses (lines 146-148, 165) but never used in layout() or draw_morphology(), and because 9 mutant joints require mean-radius padding. Evidence: 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L140–L178: Link, SubJoint, Digit, and Morphology dataclasses (including unused side/reversed/inverted fields) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L140-L178>; 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L275–L421: layout(), _edges_of(), and control_points() implementing recursive tree layout and bisector radii <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L275-L421>; 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L606–L620: check_encoding() verifies 3,137/3,146 joints match the radius rule <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L606-L620>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-lobo-limbform-morphology-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-lobo-limbform-morphology-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "LimbformDB limb morphologies — Morphometric validation: 62/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Performs an exhaustive structural audit of the database encoding in check_encoding() (verifying 555/565 geometric morphologies and 3,137/3,146 joints against the degree-radius rule), but the script itself does not compute silhouette IoU, segment-angle residuals, or landmark errors against Lobo et al. (2014b) Fig. 1 or real limb morphometrics. Evidence: 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L606–L620: check_encoding() structural verification of joint-parameter counts <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L606-L620>; 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L745–L761: main() runs check_encoding() and renders galleries without quantitative image-level comparison <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L745-L761>. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): morphologies decoded = 555 count (reference 565, rows in LimbformDB 2.1.0 Morphology table) [Morphology rows with at least one Link (segment) row] — the rest are outcome labels without geometry (Lethal, No limb, ...); joints obeying the radius rule = 3137 count (reference 3146, all joints; the rule is the formalism's (Regeneration 1:37, Fig. 2)) [joints whose JointParam count equals the number of incident segments (3 for a terminal joint; a sub-joint counts its host segment twice)]; segments, #1 Wild type, right forelimb = 3 count (reference 3, Lobo et al. 2014 Regeneration Fig. 1 A′: Upper arm, Fore arm, Hand; digits 1-4) [Link rows of the morphology]; digits, #1 Wild type, right forelimb = 4 count (reference 4, Lobo et al. 2014 Regeneration Fig. 1 A′: Upper arm, Fore arm, Hand; digits 1-4) [Digit rows of the morphology]; segments, #280 Wild type, right hindlimb = 3 count (reference 3, Lobo et al. 2014 Regeneration Fig. 1 B′: Thigh, Shank, Foot; digits 1-5 plus the prehallux node) [Link rows of the morphology]; digits, #280 Wild type, right hindlimb = 6 count (reference 6, Lobo et al. 2014 Regeneration Fig. 1 B′: Thigh, Shank, Foot; digits 1-5 plus the prehallux node) [Digit rows of the morphology]; segments, #314 Wild type, right walking leg, fiddler crab = 7 count (reference 7, Lobo et al. 2014 Regeneration Fig. 1 C′: Coxa, Basis, Ischium, Merus, Carpus, Propus, Dactyl) [Link rows of the morphology]; segments, #490 Wild type, right metathoracic (T3) leg, cricket nymph = 8 count (reference 8, Lobo et al. 2014 Regeneration Fig. 1 D′: Coxa, Trochanter, Femur, Tibia, Tarsus 1-4 (as labelled)) [Link rows of the morphology]; segments, #491 Wild type, right leg I, huntsman spider = 7 count (reference 7, Lobo et al. 2014 Regeneration Fig. 1 E′: Coxa, Trochanter, Femur, Patella, Tibia, Metatarsus, Tarsus) [Link rows of the morphology]; silhouette IoU vs Fig. 1 A'', #1 Wild type, right forelimb = 0.6448 ratio (reference 1.0, the paper's own rendering of the same database entry) [largest ink component of the cartoon panel (holes filled) and the decoded silhouette, each cropped to its bounding box and scaled to a 200-px canvas (aspect kept); intersection over union, best of 8 rotations/reflections (rot180+mirror)] — bones, digits and gradient are inside the outline, so this compares outer shape only; the cartoon is a 560-px JPEG, which bounds the achievable IoU below 1; bounding-box aspect, #1 Wild type, right forelimb = 1.5738 ratio (reference 1.463, same statistic on the Fig. 1 A'' cartoon) [longer / shorter side of the decoded silhouette's bounding box]; silhouette IoU vs Fig. 1 B'', #280 Wild type, right hindlimb = 0.4105 ratio (reference 1.0, the paper's own rendering of the same database entry) [largest ink component of the cartoon panel (holes filled) and the decoded silhouette, each cropped to its bounding box and scaled to a 200-px canvas (aspect kept); intersection over union, best of 8 rotations/reflections (rot0+mirror)] — bones, digits and gradient are inside the outline, so this compares outer shape only; the cartoon is a 560-px JPEG, which bounds the achievable IoU below 1; bounding-box aspect, #280 Wild type, right hindlimb = 1.4696 ratio (reference 1.832, same statistic on the Fig. 1 B'' cartoon) [longer / shorter side of the decoded silhouette's bounding box]; silhouette IoU vs Fig. 1 C'', #314 Wild type, right walking leg, fiddler crab = 0.4313 ratio (reference 1.0, the paper's own rendering of the same database entry) [largest ink component of the cartoon panel (holes filled) and the decoded silhouette, each cropped to its bounding box and scaled to a 200-px canvas (aspect kept); intersection over union, best of 8 rotations/reflections (rot180+mirror)] — bones, digits and gradient are inside the outline, so this compares outer shape only; the cartoon is a 560-px JPEG, which bounds the achievable IoU below 1; bounding-box aspect, #314 Wild type, right walking leg, fiddler crab = 1.2414 ratio (reference 1.051, same statistic on the Fig. 1 C'' cartoon) [longer / shorter side of the decoded silhouette's bounding box]; silhouette IoU vs Fig. 1 D'', #490 Wild type, right metathoracic (T3) leg, cricket nymph = 0.7432 ratio (reference 1.0, the paper's own rendering of the same database entry) [largest ink component of the cartoon panel (holes filled) and the decoded silhouette, each cropped to its bounding box and scaled to a 200-px canvas (aspect kept); intersection over union, best of 8 rotations/reflections (rot180+mirror)] — bones, digits and gradient are inside the outline, so this compares outer shape only; the cartoon is a 560-px JPEG, which bounds the achievable IoU below 1; bounding-box aspect, #490 Wild type, right metathoracic (T3) leg, cricket nymph = 1.1346 ratio (reference 1.084, same statistic on the Fig. 1 D'' cartoon) [longer / shorter side of the decoded silhouette's bounding box]; silhouette IoU vs Fig. 1 E'', #491 Wild type, right leg I, huntsman spider = 0.4851 ratio (reference 1.0, the paper's own rendering of the same database entry) [largest ink component of the cartoon panel (holes filled) and the decoded silhouette, each cropped to its bounding box and scaled to a 200-px canvas (aspect kept); intersection over union, best of 8 rotations/reflections (rot180+mirror)] — bones, digits and gradient are inside the outline, so this compares outer shape only; the cartoon is a 560-px JPEG, which bounds the achievable IoU below 1; bounding-box aspect, #491 Wild type, right leg I, huntsman spider = 1.5391 ratio (reference 1.455, same statistic on the Fig. 1 E'' cartoon) [longer / shorter side of the decoded silhouette's bounding box]." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-lobo-limbform-morphology-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasProbability 6.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-lobo-limbform-morphology-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "LimbformDB limb morphologies — MorphoEval overall 83.6/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Blinded second-assessor pass (gemini-4-argon). Decodes the LimbformDB 2.1.0 tree-graph schema (Morphology, Link, JointParam, LinkSubJoint, Digit) across all 565 database rows (555 with non-empty geometry) and renders smooth closed limb outlines, internal skeletal elements, and digit phalanges across 14 taxa. Independently caught a 65-hex-character typo in DB_SHA256 (line 92) that causes resolve_db_path() to emit a false-positive SHA-256 mismatch warning. Overall 83.6/100 (faithfulness 81.1, reproducibility 89.5; model-implementation 86.7/100, biological-validation 77.0/100, applicable-only overall 83.6/100; uncalibrated rubric score, not a calibrated probability); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 5659d5e; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, pandas 2.3.3, scikit-image 0.26.0, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 84, Morphometric validation 62, Source and data traceability 94, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: limbform_wildtype_gallery.png: rendered output of 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py at 5659d5e, image/png, 620043 B, 2400×1875 px, sha256 d561f4aab10756976c3fd5caf7a8c516da13c1cd9395d6cb5a54b8a2f5b10236." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-lobo-limbform-morphology> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.36e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-lobo-limbform-morphology-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "LimbformDB limb morphologies — Parameter expressivity: 84/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Exercises the full discrete and continuous variation stored in LimbformDB 2.1.0 across 555 geometric morphologies spanning 6 taxonomic classes, 14 species, 12 anatomical segment types, multi-joint branching, ectopic LinkSubJoint grafts, and 0-12 digits. Deducts 16 points because the unused Link.reversed / Link.inverted / Digit.reversed flags leave surgical handedness inversions unexpressed in the rendered geometry. Evidence: 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L222–L268: load_morphologies() loads all 565 morphologies (555 with geometry) across 14 taxa <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L222-L268>; 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L656–L676: 15 curated experimental phenotypes spanning amputations, grafts, and duplications <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L656-L676>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-lobo-limbform-morphology-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-lobo-limbform-morphology-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "LimbformDB limb morphologies — Reproducibility package: 88/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Fully deterministic geometry decoding and rendering, automatic fallback download of LimbformDB 2.1.0 into .limbform_cache/, and pinned dependencies in requirements.txt / requirements.lock.txt. Deducts 12 points for the 65-character DB_SHA256 typo in resolve_db_path() and lack of CLI flags for output paths. Evidence: 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L91–L134: resolve_db_path() auto-download and cache logic <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L91-L134>; requirements.lock.txt L1–L35: pinned environment lockfile <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/requirements.lock.txt#L1-L35>." ;
