    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-planform-morphology-animation-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Model fidelity to source: 86/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Decodes PlanformDB 2.5.0's relational tables (Morphology, Region, RegionParam, RegionsLink, Organ, OrganPoint) using the formalism's exact link-degree radius rule (0 links -> 4 cardinal radii; 1 link -> +90/+180/+270 deg; k >= 2 links -> k bisector radii), places region centres from Dist/Ang and shared borders at Ratio*Dist, and verifies in check_encoding() that 1,181/1,181 regions obey the rule. Deducts 14 points because consecutive control radii are connected by a heuristic superellipse arc (N_FREE=2.2, N_BORDER=7.0) tuned to resemble Fig. 1D rather than a closed-form curve equation published in the paper. Evidence: 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L279–L391: layout(), control_points(), and region_outline() implementing the graph-to-outline decoder <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L279-L391>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L733–L747: check_encoding() verifies 1,181/1,181 regions obey the 0->4 / 1->3 / k->k rule <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L733-L747>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-planform-morphology-animation-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Morphometric validation: 56/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Computes rasterised silhouette morphometrics (ap_length, ml_width, aspect, area, head/tail/eye/pharynx counts, and rel_wt_length) in morphometrics(), verifies wild-type dimensions against the database radii (557.6 x 119.8 vs 560 x 120 Planform units), and exports a full table via write_csv(). Held below 60 because no quantitative IoU or landmark comparison against real planarian photographs or published software screenshots is performed inside the script at commit 5659d5e. Evidence: 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L418–L444: morphometrics() computes AP length, ML width, aspect ratio, area, and organ counts <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L418-L444>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L716–L731: write_csv() exports per-morphology morphometrics <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L716-L731>. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): wild-type silhouette AP length = 557.6 Planform units (reference 560, PlanformDB 2.5.0 RegionParam/RegionsLink of morphology 1 (80+200+200+80)) [union of decoded region outlines of Morphology 1, rasterised; bbox extent along the AP axis]; wild-type silhouette ML width = 119.8 Planform units (reference 120, trunk lateral radii 60+60) [as above, across the ML axis]; wild-type AP/ML aspect = 4.653 ratio (reference 4.667, encoded radii) [AP length / ML width of the decoded silhouette] — S. mediterranea in Lobo et al. 2013 Fig. 1A is of this order; the formalism, not a specimen, is the reference; morphologies rendered = 369 count [Morphology rows with at least one encoded region] — 372 rows in the database; 3 have no regions (Lethal, Midbody Buldge, Double head, side tail); distinct body silhouettes = 167 count (reference 369, upper bound: one silhouette per morphology) [unique (AP length, ML width, area to 100 units, #heads, #tails) tuples over all rendered morphologies] — 115 morphologies share the wild-type body and differ only in organs (ectopic eyes, doubled CNS, pharynx position, ...), which is how the database encodes them; distinct encodings (regions + links + organs) = 369 count (reference 369, every morphology row is a distinct phenotype) [unique tuples of every encoded number read from the database]; IoU wild type vs double head (#24) = 0.8884 ratio (reference < 1; the two bodies differ only at the posterior cap (tail -> second head), the rest of the difference is organs) [intersection-over-union of the two decoded silhouettes on a shared canvas (region centres aligned by layout)]; IoU wild type vs headless (#20) = 0.6116 ratio (reference ≈ (trunk+tail area)/(whole-body area) if the head is simply absent) [as above]." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasProbability 5.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-planform-morphology-animation-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — MorphoEval overall 76.5/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Blinded second-assessor pass (gemini-4-argon). Decodes the Lobo, Malone & Levin (2013) region-graph formalism across all 369 geometric planarian morphologies in PlanformDB 2.5.0 (verifying the 0->4 / 1->3 / k->k radii rule on all 1,181 regions), renders 16 canonical phenotypes and a 63-frame historical morphospace timeline, and pins the database by SHA-256. Overall 76.5/100 (faithfulness 74.4, reproducibility 81.4; model-implementation 84.0/100, biological-validation 67.2/100, applicable-only overall 76.5/100; uncalibrated rubric score, not a calibrated probability); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 5659d5e; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, pandas 2.3.3, scikit-image 0.26.0, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 74, Parameter expressivity 80, Morphometric validation 56, Source and data traceability 85, Code-to-model traceability 82, Reproducibility package 78. Output judged: planform_morphology_gallery.png: rendered output of 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py at 5659d5e, image/png, 443915 B, 1920×2160 px, sha256 77a7dfa087bf89441dc35c64bc0c96bccfdc15d44a3d600df766fb723a87ace5." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.65e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-planform-morphology-animation-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
