<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-planform-morphology-animation-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Source and data traceability: 85/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Cites both primary papers (Lobo, Malone & Levin 2013 Biology Open, DOI 10.1242/bio.20123400; Bioinformatics, DOI 10.1093/bioinformatics/btt088) and pins planformDB_2.5.0.edb by exact SHA-256 digest (PLANFORM_DB_SHA256) in both the script and datasets/planform/planformDB.sha256. Deducts 15 points because the proprietary .edb file cannot be redistributed in the repository or auto-downloaded without user setup. Evidence: 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L10–L17: DOIs for both 2013 Planform papers <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L10-L17>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L147–L177: PLANFORM_DB_SHA256 and resolve_db_path() hash verification <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L147-L177>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-source-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-planform-morphology-animation-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Morphological realism / specimen match: 74/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Produces clean, immediately distinguishable Planform cartoon renderings across wild type (#1), double-head (#2, #24), headless (#20), cyclops (#14), lateral/ectopic heads (#71, #133), and multi-head phenotypes, matching the colour gradients and internal organ symbols (eyes, brain lobes, ventral nerve cords, pharynx) of Lobo et al. (2013) Fig. 1D. Deducts 26 points because the database encodes only coarse polar radii (3 per head), so species-specific triangular cephalic lobes, auricles, and pigmentation of real S. mediterranea or D. japonica specimens are absent and no worm photographs are compared in this script. Evidence: 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L492–L542: draw_morphology() renders region gradients, borders, eyes, brain, VNC, and pharynx <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L492-L542>; planform_morphology_gallery.png (generated output, not in repo): 16 canonical PlanformDB phenotypes rendered at shared scale — planform_morphology_gallery.png: rendered output of 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py at 5659d5e, image/png, 443915 B, 1920×2160 px, sha256 77a7dfa087bf89441dc35c64bc0c96bccfdc15d44a3d600df766fb723a87ace5; planform_morphospace_timeline.gif (generated output, not in repo): animated historical timeline and 359-morphology overview grid — planform_morphospace_timeline.gif: rendered output of 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py at 5659d5e, image/gif, 3265519 B, 1500×780 px, 63 frames, sha256 f7c8cadf3c06c8351a49b6a47e1fc73fafafa7b430841771c14806fe54ce92a4." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-raup-shell-coiling-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — Code-to-model traceability: 78/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "create_raup_animations.py clearly maps variables (theta, phi, a, rc, zc, r, z) to Noshita (2014) and Okabe & Yoshimura (2017). Deducts 22 points because the companion script 1966-raup.py lacks citations, docstrings, and uses a divergent formula for rc without explanation. Evidence: create_raup_animations.py L85–L131: documented raup_shell() implementation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/create_raup_animations.py#L85-L131>; 1966-raup.py L1–L56: undocumented companion script with divergent rc formula <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/1966-raup.py#L1-L56>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-raup-shell-coiling-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — Model fidelity to source: 90/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Implements the logarithmic spiral growth law a(theta) = r0 * W^(theta / 2pi), generating-curve centre distance rc(theta) = a(theta)*(1+D)/(1-D) (yielding inner/outer margin ratio (rc - a)/(rc + a) = D), axial translation zc(theta) = T * rc(theta) (so dzc/drc = T Scales with whorl radius), and aperture shape S in the meridional plane through the coiling axis, verified to ~5e-15 by recover_parameters() in self_test(). Deducts 10 points because the standalone companion script 1966-raup.py hardcodes S = 1.0 and uses an unnormalised offset rc = r*(1+D) without (1-D) scaling. Evidence: create_raup_animations.py L85–L131: raup_shell() parametric surface implementation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/create_raup_animations.py#L85-L131>; create_raup_animations.py L134–L211: recover_parameters() and self_test() verifying parameter recovery to < 1e-9 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/create_raup_animations.py#L134-L211>; 1966-raup.py L10–L29: simplified companion script with r_c = r*(1+D) and fixed circular cross-section <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/1966-raup.py#L10-L29>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-raup-shell-coiling-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — Morphometric validation: 58/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Recovers (W, D, T, S) and aspect ratios (spire_over_width, outer_radius_ratio) directly from the generated 3D vertices in recover_parameters() and exports them to raup_shell_metrics.csv (max parameter recovery error 5.33e-15). However, this validates internal mathematical self-consistency rather than comparing model outputs against empirical shell measurements from biological specimens. Evidence: create_raup_animations.py L134–L211: recover_parameters() and self_test() geometric verification <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/create_raup_animations.py#L134-L211>; raup_shell_metrics.csv L1–L8: exported input vs mesh-recovered parameter table <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/raup_shell_metrics.csv#L1-L8>. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): recovered translation rate T, 'Planispiral' (W=3.0, D=0.0, T=0.0) = 0.0 ratio (reference 0.0, Raup's definition of T (dz_c/dr_c), Noshita 2014 / Okabe & Yoshimura 2017; should equal the input) [Δz_c / Δr_c of the generating-curve centre over the last revolution of raup_shell()] — height/width = 0.629, spire/width = 0.000; recovered distance from axis D, 'Planispiral' (W=3.0, D=0.0, T=0.0) = 0.0003 ratio (reference 0.0, Raup's definition of D; should equal the input) [inner margin / outer margin of the aperture (min/max radial distance of the last generating curve)]; recovered whorl expansion W, 'Planispiral' (W=3.0, D=0.0, T=0.0) = 3.0 ratio (reference 3.0, Raup's definition of W; should equal the input) [centre distance from the axis at the aperture / one revolution earlier]; recovered translation rate T, 'Turreted' (W=1.3, D=0.05, T=3.5) = 3.5 ratio (reference 3.5, Raup's definition of T (dz_c/dr_c), Noshita 2014 / Okabe & Yoshimura 2017; should equal the input) [Δz_c / Δr_c of the generating-curve centre over the last revolution of raup_shell()] — height/width = 1.142, spire/width = 0.858; recovered distance from axis D, 'Turreted' (W=1.3, D=0.05, T=3.5) = 0.0502 ratio (reference 0.05, Raup's definition of D; should equal the input) [inner margin / outer margin of the aperture (min/max radial distance of the last generating curve)]; recovered whorl expansion W, 'Turreted' (W=1.3, D=0.05, T=3.5) = 1.3 ratio (reference 1.3, Raup's definition of W; should equal the input) [centre distance from the axis at the aperture / one revolution earlier]; recovered translation rate T, 'Evolute disc' (W=2.0, D=0.45, T=0.0) = 0.0 ratio (reference 0.0, Raup's definition of T (dz_c/dr_c), Noshita 2014 / Okabe & Yoshimura 2017; should equal the input) [Δz_c / Δr_c of the generating-curve centre over the last revolution of raup_shell()] — height/width = 0.321, spire/width = 0.000; recovered distance from axis D, 'Evolute disc' (W=2.0, D=0.45, T=0.0) = 0.4501 ratio (reference 0.45, Raup's definition of D; should equal the input) [inner margin / outer margin of the aperture (min/max radial distance of the last generating curve)]; recovered whorl expansion W, 'Evolute disc' (W=2.0, D=0.45, T=0.0) = 2.0 ratio (reference 2.0, Raup's definition of W; should equal the input) [centre distance from the axis at the aperture / one revolution earlier]; recovered translation rate T, 'Conical' (W=3.5, D=0.0, T=1.5) = 1.5 ratio (reference 1.5, Raup's definition of T (dz_c/dr_c), Noshita 2014 / Okabe & Yoshimura 2017; should equal the input) [Δz_c / Δr_c of the generating-curve centre over the last revolution of raup_shell()] — height/width = 0.805, spire/width = 0.481; recovered distance from axis D, 'Conical' (W=3.5, D=0.0, T=1.5) = 0.0003 ratio (reference 0.0, Raup's definition of D; should equal the input) [inner margin / outer margin of the aperture (min/max radial distance of the last generating curve)]; recovered whorl expansion W, 'Conical' (W=3.5, D=0.0, T=1.5) = 3.5 ratio (reference 3.5, Raup's definition of W; should equal the input) [centre distance from the axis at the aperture / one revolution earlier]; recovered translation rate T, 'High-spired' (W=1.6, D=0.1, T=2.5) = 2.5 ratio (reference 2.5, Raup's definition of T (dz_c/dr_c), Noshita 2014 / Okabe & Yoshimura 2017; should equal the input) [Δz_c / Δr_c of the generating-curve centre over the last revolution of raup_shell()] — height/width = 0.998, spire/width = 0.738; recovered distance from axis D, 'High-spired' (W=1.6, D=0.1, T=2.5) = 0.1002 ratio (reference 0.1, Raup's definition of D; should equal the input) [inner margin / outer margin of the aperture (min/max radial distance of the last generating curve)]; recovered whorl expansion W, 'High-spired' (W=1.6, D=0.1, T=2.5) = 1.6 ratio (reference 1.6, Raup's definition of W; should equal the input) [centre distance from the axis at the aperture / one revolution earlier]; recovered translation rate T, 'Globose' (W=3.0, D=0.1, T=1.0) = 1.0 ratio (reference 1.0, Raup's definition of T (dz_c/dr_c), Noshita 2014 / Okabe & Yoshimura 2017; should equal the input) [Δz_c / Δr_c of the generating-curve centre over the last revolution of raup_shell()] — height/width = 0.628, spire/width = 0.341; recovered distance from axis D, 'Globose' (W=3.0, D=0.1, T=1.0) = 0.1002 ratio (reference 0.1, Raup's definition of D; should equal the input) [inner margin / outer margin of the aperture (min/max radial distance of the last generating curve)]; recovered whorl expansion W, 'Globose' (W=3.0, D=0.1, T=1.0) = 3.0 ratio (reference 3.0, Raup's definition of W; should equal the input) [centre distance from the axis at the aperture / one revolution earlier]." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasProbability 5.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-raup-shell-coiling-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — MorphoEval overall 79.3/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Blinded second-assessor pass (gemini-4-argon). Implements Raup's (1962, 1966) four-parameter logarithmic-spiral shell model (W, D, T, S) using the parametric surface formulation of Noshita (2014) and Okabe & Yoshimura (2017), with an automated self_test() that recovers (W, D, T, S) from the 3D mesh to machine precision (~5e-15). Overall 79.3/100 (faithfulness 76.4, reproducibility 86.1; model-implementation 86.0/100, biological-validation 69.2/100, applicable-only overall 79.3/100; uncalibrated rubric score, not a calibrated probability); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 5659d5e; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, pandas 2.3.3, scikit-image 0.26.0, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 76, Parameter expressivity 78, Morphometric validation 58, Source and data traceability 82, Code-to-model traceability 78, Reproducibility package 95. Output judged: raup_shell_animation.gif: rendered output of create_raup_animations.py at 5659d5e, image/gif, 15189434 B, 1200×800 px, 100 frames, sha256 986555a0032be189233cbf0ec15193959bf7f9cc0b1e099a6b7a289f7cff8b02." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.93e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-raup-shell-coiling-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — Parameter expressivity: 78/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Covers wide ranges of W (1.6 to 10.0), D (0.02 to 0.55), and T (0.0 to 4.2) across the 6-panel comparison and 120-frame morphing animation. Deducts 22 points because S is held constant at 1.0 in every rendered figure and JSON preset, and create_parameter_space_visualization() zips three values of W with three values of D (and W with T) along a 1D diagonal (3 panels per row) rather than sampling a 2D (W, D) or (W, T) morphospace grid. Evidence: create_raup_animations.py L289–L344: create_parameter_space_visualization() zips 3 (W, D) and 3 (W, T) pairs with S=1.0 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/create_raup_animations.py#L289-L344>; datasets/raup/variables.json L30–L85: all six parameter sets set S = 1.0 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/datasets/raup/variables.json#L30-L85>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-raup-shell-coiling-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — Reproducibility package: 95/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Completely deterministic mathematical surface generation, zero external network dependencies, automated self_test() gate executed before rendering, and pinned dependencies in requirements.txt / requirements.lock.txt. Evidence: create_raup_animations.py L443–L459: main() runs self_test() and generates all four outputs deterministically <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/create_raup_animations.py#L443-L459>; requirements.lock.txt L1–L35: pinned environment lockfile <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/requirements.lock.txt#L1-L35>." ;
