    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling-repro-package> ;
    pk:hasProbability 9.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-raup-shell-coiling-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — Source and data traceability: 82/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Cites Raup (1962, 1965, 1966, 1967) and the two secondary papers from which the exact parametric equations were taken (Noshita 2014, DOI 10.1016/j.jtbi.2014.08.010; Okabe & Yoshimura 2017, DOI 10.1038/srep42445), and transparently documents in both the script and datasets/raup/variables.json that Raup (1966) was not consulted directly and that earlier AI-fabricated page citations were retracted. Evidence: create_raup_animations.py L1–L35: module docstring citing Raup (1962, 1965, 1966) and Noshita (2014) / Okabe & Yoshimura (2017) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/create_raup_animations.py#L1-L35>; datasets/raup/variables.json L1–L29: provenance note retracting earlier unverified page numbers <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/datasets/raup/variables.json#L1-L29>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling-source-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-raup-shell-coiling-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — Morphological realism / specimen match: 76/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Renders six distinct shell archetypes (planispiral involute cf. Nautilus, high-spired turreted cf. Turritella, evolute planispiral cf. Dactylioceras, low-spired obconical cf. Conus, medium-spired cf. Cerithium, helicoid globose cf. Helix) whose 3D geometries and spire-height/width ratios (0.00 to 2.26) match their morphological descriptions. Deducts 24 points because no real mollusc shell photograph, CT scan, or empirical specimen dataset (such as Raup 1967) is overlaid or compared, and the six parameter sets are explicitly declared as illustrative \"cf.\" points rather than measurements of real specimens. Evidence: datasets/raup/variables.json L18–L86: six illustrative shell parameter sets with honest provenance note <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/datasets/raup/variables.json#L18-L86>; raup_empirical_comparison.png (generated output, not in repo): 6-panel 3D comparison of coiled shell archetypes — raup_empirical_comparison.png: rendered output of create_raup_animations.py at 5659d5e, image/png, 562658 B, 1630×1070 px, sha256 c50dbee57d0a64950d5470aed25583817eb8d39b97bcf2a7b89b991973f63ef7; raup_shell_metrics.csv L1–L8: spire_over_width and outer_radius_ratio across the six archetypes <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/raup_shell_metrics.csv#L1-L8>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-santella-wormguides-celegans-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "WormGUIDES C. elegans embryo atlas with the OpenWorm connectome — Code-to-model traceability: 82/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Explicitly documents the WormGUIDES Java loader class (AceTreeTableLineageDataLoader), ProductionInfo.csv and CellShapesConfig.csv fields, Sulston regex grammar, and literature check constants inline where they are used. Evidence: 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L113–L124: LIT benchmark dictionary and SULSTON_RE <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L113-L124>; 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L254–L275: read_nuclei() and movie_offset() mapped to WormGUIDES loader <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L254-L275>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-santella-wormguides-celegans-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-santella-wormguides-celegans-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "WormGUIDES C. elegans embryo atlas with the OpenWorm connectome — Model fidelity to source: 84/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Accurately decodes StarryNite/AceTree nuclei tables following AceTreeTableLineageDataLoader column conventions, parses time offsets from ProductionInfo.csv, verifies the Sulston naming grammar on all 1,330 cell names and parent-before-child ordering on 1,326/1,326 cells, reconstructs the lineage bifurcation tree directly from cell names, and calibrates spatial coordinates using the re-segmented frame-330 eggshell mesh (50 um / 303.1 units = 0.1649 um/unit). Deducts 16 points because the 3D embryo and 51 single-cell OBJ meshes are rendered as 2D orthographic projections rather than full 3D surfaces, and the c302 connectome is collapsed into a single summed adjacency matrix without separating chemical synapses from gap junctions. Evidence: 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L254–L319: read_nuclei(), movie_offset(), founder(), parent_of(), and check_encoding() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L254-L319>; 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L335–L368: calibrate(), shell_report(), and nuclear_cloud_scale() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L335-L368>; 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L564–L595: canonical_cell() and draw_connectome() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L564-L595>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-santella-wormguides-celegans-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-santella-wormguides-celegans-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "WormGUIDES C. elegans embryo atlas with the OpenWorm connectome — Morphometric validation: 82/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Validates decoded atlas metrics against Sulston et al. (1983) / WormAtlas and Cook et al. (2019) benchmarks: 1,330/1,330 valid Sulston names, 1,326/1,326 parent-before-child appearances, 113/113 programmed cell deaths present, unfitted eggshell width of 29.24 um against the 30 um reference (and 13-mesh scale bracket 0.1649-0.1750 um/unit), 562-571 nuclei at 330-350 min (vs ~550), E-cell gastrulation ingression at 26 cells (vs ~30-cell stage), and 300/302 hermaphrodite neurons (with CANL/CANR explained by lack of synapses). Also quantifies and reports the 19.0-unit static-shell overrun and the ~27-minute clock offset at gastrulation (73 min vs 100 min). Evidence: 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L348–L423: shell_report(), measure(), gastrulation_onset(), and literature_checks() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L348-L423>; celegans_four_views.png (generated output, not in repo): annotated morphometric and lineage benchmarks — celegans_four_views.png: rendered output of 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py at 5659d5e, image/png, 424197 B, 2240×1680 px, sha256 eb4b60086280c9a1740358c26fc655598f25d2adad63a9fcdb9c3a7980cc3bd6. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): lineage names parsing as Sulston names = 1330 count (reference 1330, all distinct names in the atlas) [distinct names in the 360 nuclei files matching ^(AB|MS|E|C|D|EMS|P[0-4]|Z[23])[aplrdv]*$]; cells first seen after their parent = 1326 count (reference 1326, all cells whose parent is in the movie (4 founders present at frame 1 have parents that predate it)) [non-founder cells whose parent name appears in an earlier frame]; calibration = 0.1649 µm per atlas unit [x extent of the atlas's eggshell outline mesh at frame 330 (obj_files/embryo_t330.obj, 'Embryo Outline' in CellShapesConfig.csv; 303.1 units) set to the 50 µm egg length] — assumption: Gönczy et al. 1999 JCB 144:927 ('50-µm-long cell'); the atlas coordinates are unit-less (ProductionInfo X/Y/Z_SCALE = 1); the earlier nuclear-cloud estimate gives 0.1617; the sampled shell meshes give 0.1649-0.1750; eggshell width under the calibration = 29.238 µm (reference 30.0, Gönczy et al. 1999 JCB 144:927 / WormAtlas: the egg is ~50 x 30 µm) [y extent of the eggshell outline mesh at frame 330 (z extent 28.9 µm)] — a consistency check of the calibration: the width is not fitted; eggshell length spread across sampled shell meshes = 17.3733 atlas units [max - min x extent of the eggshell meshes at frames [1, 30, 60, 100, 200, 250, 280, 300, 320, 330, 340, 350, 359] (285.8-303.1)] — one static mesh is reused for frames 1-~250, re-segmented per frame from ~280; the spread bounds the scale uncertainty (~6 %); nuclear overrun of the shell in x = 19.0129 atlas units [largest distance by which a nucleus (centroid ± radius) lies outside the shell mesh's x range at the sampled frames] — 1.8 units at frame 330; the overrun is against the static early mesh, which is why the calibration uses the re-segmented shell; nuclear cloud width at the last frame = 27.28 µm [y span of nuclear centroids + one mean diameter under the calibration] — nuclei do not reach the eggshell; compare the eggshell width above; nuclei at the last frame = 580 count (reference 558, WormAtlas, Embryo introduction (Sulston et al. 1983), accessed 2026-10-15: 558 cells at hatching (671 generated, 113 deaths)) [valid rows of t360-nuclei (movie-minute 379)] — the movie ends before hatching; 553 of the 580 nuclei carry a parts-list identity; maximum nucleus count = 585 count (reference 550, WormAtlas, Embryo introduction (Sulston et al. 1983), accessed 2026-10-15: ~550 cells at the end of proliferation (330-350 min)) [maximum over the 360 frames]; deaths listed by the atlas = 113 count (reference 113, WormAtlas, Embryo introduction (Sulston et al. 1983), accessed 2026-10-15: 113 embryonic cell deaths) [names in CellDeaths.csv]; listed dying cells that occur in the movie = 113 count (reference 113) [CellDeaths.csv names present in at least one nuclei file]; gastrulation onset, cell count = 26 count (reference 30, WormAtlas, Embryo introduction (Sulston et al. 1983), accessed 2026-10-15: ~30-cell stage (26-28 cells when Ea/Ep ingress)) [first frame from which the E cells sit at < 0.8 of the median normalised radius for 5 frames]; gastrulation onset, movie-minute = 73 min (reference 100, WormAtlas, Embryo introduction (Sulston et al. 1983), accessed 2026-10-15: Ea/Ep enter the embryo at 100 min after first cleavage) [same frame, frame index + movie start offset] — discrepancy: the atlas clock runs ~27 min ahead of the Sulston schedule at the same cell stage; not resolved by the script (temperature or time origin); nuclei at movie-minute 330-350 = 562-571 count (reference 550, WormAtlas, Embryo introduction (Sulston et al. 1983), accessed 2026-10-15: ~550 cells at 330-350 min) [nucleus count over that window]; neurons in the connectome edge list = 300 count (reference 302, Cook et al. 2019 / White et al. 1986: 302 hermaphrodite neurons) [upper-case node names of c302 herm_full_edgelist.csv after DA01->DA1 canonicalisation] — CANL/CANR are 'no synapses' in the WormGUIDES parts list and so cannot appear in an edge list." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-santella-wormguides-celegans-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-santella-wormguides-celegans-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "WormGUIDES C. elegans embryo atlas with the OpenWorm connectome — MorphoEval overall 78.7/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Blinded second-assessor pass (gemini-4-argon). Decodes 360 frames of 3D nuclear coordinates and diameters from the WormGUIDES C. elegans embryogenesis atlas (Santella et al. 2015), verifies Sulston lineage naming and parent-before-child ordering across all 1,330 cells, calibrates spatial units against the frame-330 eggshell OBJ mesh (0.1649 um/unit), documents the static early shell mesh overrun, and pairs the developmental atlas with the OpenWorm c302 hermaphrodite connectome (300 neurons). Overall 78.7/100 (faithfulness 75.1, reproducibility 86.9; model-implementation 72.7/100, biological-validation 77.0/100, applicable-only overall 81.9/100; uncalibrated rubric score, not a calibrated probability); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 5659d5e; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, pandas 2.3.3, scikit-image 0.26.0, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 84, Morphological realism / specimen match 74, Parameter expressivity 50, Morphometric validation 82, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 82, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: celegans_four_views.png: rendered output of 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py at 5659d5e, image/png, 424197 B, 2240×1680 px, sha256 eb4b60086280c9a1740358c26fc655598f25d2adad63a9fcdb9c3a7980cc3bd6." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-santella-wormguides-celegans> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.87e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

