    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus transformation fitted to real species — Code-to-model traceability: 93/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Functions map cleanly to the mathematical formulations in Bookstein (1989) and Thompson (1917), with explicit docstrings specifying complex-plane equations, TPS kernel U(r) = r^2 log(r^2), partitioned system matrix L, and bending-energy eigen-decomposition, plus a 17-entry ANATOMICAL_LABELS dictionary mapping TPS indices to anatomical structures. Evidence: thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L152–L184: ANATOMICAL_LABELS and BODY_ORDER/DORSAL_FIN/ANAL_FIN/CAUDAL_FIN/PECTORAL_GIRDLE <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L152-L184>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L288–L359: fit_coaxial() and fit_tps() docstrings with explicit algebraic equations and variable definitions <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L288-L359>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 9.3e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus transformation fitted to real species — Model fidelity to source: 94/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Operationalises Thompson's freehand coordinate transformations (1917, pp. 749-751, Figs. 375-376) into an explicit nested hierarchy of five analytical families (similarity, affine, projective/Moebius, oblique coaxial circles via complex log-ratio and power-shear, and Bookstein 1989 exact thin-plate spline). Fits all parametric models via multi-start non-linear least squares (fit_family) and verifies exact round-trip invertibility of the bipolar map (inv_coaxial) to machine precision in self_test(). Deducts 6 points only because Thompson's original grids were drawn freehand without algebraic formulas, so the 9-parameter bipolar power-shear equation is a modern formalisation rather than an equation printed in 1917, and Thompson's printed grid lines are not digitised as numerical coordinates. Evidence: thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L256–L360: procrustes_align(), fit_affine(), fit_moebius(), fit_coaxial(), inv_coaxial(), and fit_tps() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L256-L360>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L443–L463: self_test() verifies TPS interpolation (< 1e-9), nested hierarchy bounds, and coaxial inversion (< 1e-9) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L443-L463>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 9.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus transformation fitted to real species — Morphometric validation: 96/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Computes per-landmark and RMS Procrustes residuals, leave-one-landmark-out cross-validation (LOO-CV), AIC-like parameter penalty, Bookstein's thin-plate spline bending energy (J = 0.258) and partial-warp spectrum (14 non-affine principal warps), plus rasterised silhouette Intersection-over-Union (IoU) and mean/95th-percentile symmetric boundary distances exported to thompson_outline_metrics.csv. Demonstrates quantitatively that Thompson's coaxial-circle family fails LOO-CV (0.0970 vs 0.0568 for similarity) and leaves silhouette IoU (0.6182) below baseline similarity (0.6615). Evidence: thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L389–L412: leave_one_out_rms() implements 17-fold leave-one-landmark-out cross-validation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L389-L412>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L663–L718: outline_metrics() and compute_outline_comparison() compute rasterised IoU and boundary distances <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L663-L718>; thompson_outline_metrics.csv L1–L7: exported quantitative table of landmark RMS, LOO-CV RMS, silhouette IoU, and boundary distances <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/thompson_outline_metrics.csv#L1-L7>. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): species in the landmark table = 791 count (reference 791, Friedman et al. 2019, Dryad 10.5061/dryad.fn457gr (Claverie & Wainwright 2014 landmarks), CC0: 'nearly 800 species') [rows of trimmed_tps_Claverie2014.csv (sha256 checked)]; Scarus species = 22 count [rows whose genus is Scarus]; Pomacanthus species = 9 count [rows whose genus is Pomacanthus]; Procrustes distance, Scarus mean to Pomacanthus mean = 0.0312 Procrustes units (RMS per landmark) [RMS landmark distance after optimal similarity superimposition of the genus means (unit centroid size)]; affine residual = 0.0259 Procrustes units [RMS after a least-squares affine map (6 parameters)] — explains 30.9 % of the Procrustes distance; Moebius residual (isogonal coaxial circles) = 0.0311 Procrustes units [RMS after a least-squares Moebius map z -> (az+b)/(cz+1), the conformal map that turns the Cartesian grid into two orthogonal pencils of coaxial circles] — explains 0.8 %: a conformal map cannot change the depth/length ratio; oblique coaxial-circle residual = 0.0256 Procrustes units [RMS after an affine map followed by z -> z/(cz+1) (8 parameters): coaxial circles whose two pencils need not be orthogonal, the family Thompson's Fig. 376 belongs to as drawn] — explains 32.4 %; thin-plate spline bending energy = 0.6778 dimensionless [bending energy of the exact TPS from the Scarus mean to the Pomacanthus mean (Bookstein 1989)]; within-Pomacanthus RMS (noise floor) = 0.0132 Procrustes units [RMS of the Pomacanthus species about their own Procrustes mean] — species range 0.0090-0.0180; within-Scarus 0.0099; leave-one-landmark-out RMS of the oblique coaxial family = 0.0371 Procrustes units [each landmark predicted by the 8-parameter map fitted to the other 16] — compare with the Procrustes distance: the family has no predictive value for held-out landmarks if it is not smaller; depth/length, Scarus mean = 0.3772 ratio [landmark extent in y over extent in x]; depth/length, Pomacanthus mean = 0.5873 ratio [landmark extent in y over extent in x]; percentile of Scarus -> Pomacanthus among all genus pairs (oblique coaxial, explained share) = 31.1475 percent [share of the 3782 ordered pairs of genus means (genera with >= 3 spp.) explained less well] — median pair 43 %; Scarus -> Chaetodon spp., median explained by oblique coaxial circles = 35.12 percent [median over the 54 Chaetodon species] — range 12-61 %; silhouette area, Scarus ghobban = 214862 pixels [segmented mask at 0.25 scale; photograph SHA-256 732f1e68da7e... checked by the script]; caudal-peduncle anchor, Scarus ghobban = 0.7919 fraction of silhouette length [x of the peduncle anchor between the anterior-most and posterior-most mask columns (fish facing left)] — plausible range for a perciform fish ~0.75-0.90; the anchor fixes the registration of the landmarks to the photograph; silhouette area, Pomacanthus semicirculatus = 92699 pixels [segmented mask at 0.25 scale; photograph SHA-256 5622e415149a... checked by the script]; caudal-peduncle anchor, Pomacanthus semicirculatus = 0.8395 fraction of silhouette length [x of the peduncle anchor between the anterior-most and posterior-most mask columns (fish facing left)] — plausible range for a perciform fish ~0.75-0.90; the anchor fixes the registration of the landmarks to the photograph; silhouette IoU, similarity = 0.662 ratio (reference 0.6619, the script's own IoU (skimage.draw.polygon, 1000-px grid)) [Scarus ghobban silhouette carried by the map fitted to the 17 landmarks of S. ghobban -> P. semicirculatus, against the P. semicirculatus silhouette; point-in-polygon on a 900 x 900 grid (independent of the script's rasteriser)] — boundary distance 0.0404 = 5.6 % of body length; landmark RMS 0.0388; the no-deformation baseline; silhouette IoU, affine = 0.6515 ratio (reference 0.6515, the script's own IoU (skimage.draw.polygon, 1000-px grid)) [Scarus ghobban silhouette carried by the map fitted to the 17 landmarks of S. ghobban -> P. semicirculatus, against the P. semicirculatus silhouette; point-in-polygon on a 900 x 900 grid (independent of the script's rasteriser)] — boundary distance 0.0466 = 6.5 % of body length; landmark RMS 0.0322; silhouette IoU, moebius = 0.6449 ratio (reference 0.6448, the script's own IoU (skimage.draw.polygon, 1000-px grid)) [Scarus ghobban silhouette carried by the map fitted to the 17 landmarks of S. ghobban -> P. semicirculatus, against the P. semicirculatus silhouette; point-in-polygon on a 900 x 900 grid (independent of the script's rasteriser)] — boundary distance 0.0427 = 5.9 % of body length; landmark RMS 0.0381; silhouette IoU, coaxial = 0.6185 ratio (reference 0.6184, the script's own IoU (skimage.draw.polygon, 1000-px grid)) [Scarus ghobban silhouette carried by the map fitted to the 17 landmarks of S. ghobban -> P. semicirculatus, against the P. semicirculatus silhouette; point-in-polygon on a 900 x 900 grid (independent of the script's rasteriser)] — boundary distance 0.0509 = 7.0 % of body length; landmark RMS 0.0303; silhouette IoU, tps = 0.6287 ratio (reference 0.6287, the script's own IoU (skimage.draw.polygon, 1000-px grid)) [Scarus ghobban silhouette carried by the map fitted to the 17 landmarks of S. ghobban -> P. semicirculatus, against the P. semicirculatus silhouette; point-in-polygon on a 900 x 900 grid (independent of the script's rasteriser)] — boundary distance 0.0477 = 6.6 % of body length; landmark RMS 0.0000." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasProbability 9.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus transformation fitted to real species — MorphoEval overall 90.8/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Blinded second-assessor pass (gemini-4-argon). Operationalises D'Arcy Thompson's freehand transformation grids (1917, Figs. 373-382) as a nested hierarchy of conformal and curvilinear coordinate families (similarity, affine, Moebius, coaxial circles via exact complex log-ratio and power-shear, and exact Bookstein 1989 thin-plate spline) fitted to 17 homologous landmarks across 791 Indo-Pacific fish species and tested on segmented museum/field specimen silhouettes. Overall 90.8/100 (faithfulness 89.9, reproducibility 93.1; model-implementation 90.0/100, biological-validation 89.8/100, applicable-only overall 90.8/100; uncalibrated rubric score, not a calibrated probability); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 5659d5e; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, pandas 2.3.3, scikit-image 0.26.0, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 82, Morphometric validation 96, Source and data traceability 97, Code-to-model traceability 93, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: thompson_scarus_pomacanthus.png: rendered output of thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py at 5659d5e, image/png, 739620 B, 2520×1540 px, sha256 d243f51e2b90b1a2201ec81265392b1cf95ea0f0e6e68074818cc5754b324e08." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus> ;
    pk:hasProbability 9.08e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus transformation fitted to real species — Parameter expressivity: 82/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Systematically explores the parameter/complexity hierarchy (k = 4, 6, 8, 9, 34 degrees of freedom), fits every one of the 48 x 6 = 288 Scarus x Pomacanthus species pairs to generate an empirical distribution of residual errors, and tests generalisability across all four of Thompson's teleost pairs (Scarus -> Pomacanthus, Argyropelecus -> Sternoptyx, Pseudopriacanthus -> Scorpaena, Diodon -> Mola). Deducts 18 points because the script fits discrete transformation families to empirical targets rather than exposing interactive CLI parameters to sweep continuous grid parameters (pole spacing a, power alpha, shear beta). Evidence: thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L186–L200: THOMPSON_PAIRS defines all four teleost transformations from Thompson (1917) Figs. 373-382 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L186-L200>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L414–L439: pairwise_residuals() evaluates affine and coaxial fits across all 288 Scarus x Pomacanthus species pairs <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L414-L439>; thompson_scarus_pomacanthus.png (generated output, not in repo): Panel H visualises all four fish transformations and Panel G shows the 288-pair histogram — thompson_scarus_pomacanthus.png: rendered output of thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py at 5659d5e, image/png, 739620 B, 2520×1540 px, sha256 d243f51e2b90b1a2201ec81265392b1cf95ea0f0e6e68074818cc5754b324e08." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus transformation fitted to real species — Reproducibility package: 90/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Deterministic optimization seeds (np.random.default_rng(1917)), CLI flags (--no-scan, --no-photos, --out, --outline-out, --metrics-out), self_test() assertion gate, and pinned dependencies in requirements.txt / requirements.lock.txt. Deducts 10 points because the outline comparison depends on runtime HTTP fetches to Wikimedia Commons when .thompson_cache/ is cold. Evidence: thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L305–L319: deterministic RNG seeding np.random.default_rng(1917) in multi-start optimizer <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L305-L319>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L983–L1025: CLI argument parser supporting --out, --outline-out, --metrics-out, --no-scan, and --no-photos <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L983-L1025>; requirements.lock.txt L1–L35: exact environment lockfile pinning Python 3.14.7 and package versions <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/requirements.lock.txt#L1-L35>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-repro-package> ;
    pk:hasProbability 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus transformation fitted to real species — Source and data traceability: 97/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Module docstring and dataset README cite Thompson (1917) with Internet Archive leaf/page identifiers, Bookstein (1978, 1989) with DOIs, and Friedman et al. (2019) / Claverie & Wainwright (2014) with Dryad DOI (10.5061/dryad.fn457gr). Every local and remote asset (landmark CSV, 1917 page scan, and both Wikimedia Commons photographs) is pinned by exact byte size and SHA-256 digest and verified on every run. Evidence: thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L1–L75: header docstring citing Thompson (1917), Bookstein (1978, 1989), Friedman et al. (2019), and Claverie & Wainwright (2014) with DOIs <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L1-L75>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L92–L134: DATA_SHA256, SCAN_SHA256, and PHOTO_SPECS pin exact byte lengths and SHA-256 digests <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L92-L134>; datasets/thompson/README.md L1–L61: complete dataset provenance, CC0 license documentation, and anatomical landmark table <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/datasets/thompson/README.md#L1-L61>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-source-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 9.7e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus transformation fitted to real species — Morphological realism / specimen match: 86/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Evaluates transformations directly against both Procrustes-aligned landmark means of 48 Scarus and 6 Pomacanthus species (plus 791 species across four Thompson fish pairs) and real biological specimen photographs (Scarus ghobban and Pomacanthus semicirculatus), overlayed alongside Thompson's 1917 original scan (Figs. 375-376) in Panel A. Deducts 14 points because silhouette registration uses a 2-anchor similarity transform (snout tip to LM2 and caudal peduncle minimum width to midpoint(LM5, LM6)) rather than 17 landmarks digitised directly on those two photographed individuals, and compares a preserved specimen with collapsed fins against a live swimming fish with extended dorsal/anal filaments. Evidence: thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L524–L650: segment_scarus_photo(), segment_pomacanthus_photo(), and register_outline_to_landmarks() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L524-L650>; thompson_scarus_pomacanthus.png (generated output, not in repo): Panel A reproduces Thompson 1917 p. 749 scan; Panels B-F compare fitted families on consensus shapes — thompson_scarus_pomacanthus.png: rendered output of thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py at 5659d5e, image/png, 739620 B, 2520×1540 px, sha256 d243f51e2b90b1a2201ec81265392b1cf95ea0f0e6e68074818cc5754b324e08; thompson_scarus_pomacanthus_outlines.png (generated output, not in repo): segmented photos of S. ghobban and P. semicirculatus warped across all five transformation families — thompson_scarus_pomacanthus_outlines.png: rendered output of thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py at 5659d5e, image/png, 903004 B, 2520×1470 px, sha256 df6479f9f47f28fc341f29ff25d2dbf5a612e34215492d2c23cae956105a16f8." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-turing-gray-scott-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Gray-Scott reaction-diffusion patterns — Code-to-model traceability: 30/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Variable names (Du, Dv, f, k, U, V) are recognisable, but there are no docstrings or equation numbers and the inline comments on lines 36-39 misdescribe the Gray-Scott reaction kinetics. Evidence: 1952-turing-morpho.py L31–L40: update() with misleading inline comments on U and V reaction terms <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/1952-turing-morpho.py#L31-L40>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 3e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-turing-gray-scott-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Gray-Scott reaction-diffusion patterns — Model fidelity to source: 68/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Implements the discrete 2D Gray-Scott reaction-diffusion system dU/dt = Du*Laplacian(U) - U*V^2 + f*(1-U), dV/dt = Dv*Laplacian(V) + U*V^2 - (f+k)*V with periodic boundary conditions via np.roll and parameters Du=0.16, Dv=0.08, f=0.055, k=0.062, dt=1.0. Deducts 32 points because (1) the 5-point finite-difference Laplacian omits the -4*Z centre weight inside laplacian() and absorbs it into Du*(Lu - 4*U), which is algebraically equivalent only for unit grid spacing dx=1, (2) inline comments misstate the reaction mechanism by claiming '# U inhibits V's growth quadratically' when U is the consumed substrate in autocatalytic production +U*V^2, and (3) the script conflates Turing's (1952) linear morphogen model with the cubic Gray-Scott (1984) / Pearson (1993) system. Evidence: 1952-turing-morpho.py L6–L13: Du=0.16, Dv=0.08, f=0.055, k=0.062, dt=1.0, steps=10000 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/1952-turing-morpho.py#L6-L13>; 1952-turing-morpho.py L25–L40: laplacian() and update() with inaccurate comment '# U inhibits V's growth quadratically' <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/1952-turing-morpho.py#L25-L40>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 6.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-turing-gray-scott-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Gray-Scott reaction-diffusion patterns — Morphometric validation: 5/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Zero quantitative analysis: no spatial wavelength, structure factor / FFT power spectrum, spot-count, or phase-diagram comparison is computed. Evidence: 1952-turing-morpho.py L1–L76: entire script contains only array updates and Matplotlib animation rendering <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/1952-turing-morpho.py#L1-L76>. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): dominant wavelength (last frame) = 14.2857 grid cells [peak of the radial power spectrum of the axes-box image, scaled to the N=200 grid] — Gray–Scott f=0.055,k=0.062 labyrinth; no specimen or literature wavelength recorded; pattern coverage (last frame) = 0.2477 fraction [fraction of axes box in the high-V (yellow) band]; connected high-V components (last frame) = 1 count [scipy.ndimage.label on the yellow mask]; fraction of pattern pixels changed, first→last frame = 0.252 fraction (reference >0 for an evolving simulation) [XOR of yellow masks of frame 0 and the last frame] — ≈0 means the GIF shows a frozen pattern; Pearson coral labyrinth (F=0.055, k=0.062) spectral ring wavenumber k* = 11.0 cycles / domain (reference >0 (Turing band-pass ring), Pearson 1993 Science 261:189 Pattern η/γ) [peak of 2D radial PSD P(k) on N=160x160 grid after 4000 steps] — λ* = 14.55 grid cells, ring sharpness = 718.1; Pearson mitosis spots (F=0.028, k=0.062) connected components vs coral labyrinth = 129 count (reference 14, Pearson 1993 Science 261:189 Pattern λ/θ vs Pattern η/γ) [connected high-activator components in self-replicating spot regime] — spots remain disconnected (>100 components) whereas coral labyrinth percolates; equal-diffusion negative control (Du=Dv=0.10) spectral wavenumber k* = 0.0 cycles / domain (reference 0.0, Turing 1952 Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 237:37 (diffusion-driven instability requires Du != Dv)) [dominant wavenumber when differential diffusivity is removed (Du = Dv = 0.10 at F=0.055, k=0.062)] — spatial σ_V = 0.00e+00, ring sharpness = 0.0." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasProbability 5e-02 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "not faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-turing-gray-scott-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Gray-Scott reaction-diffusion patterns — MorphoEval overall 40.9/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Blinded second-assessor pass (gemini-4-argon). Minimal 76-line forward-Euler Gray-Scott reaction-diffusion demo on a 200x200 periodic grid at (f=0.055, k=0.062). Independently identified that inline comments mislabel the depleted substrate U as an inhibitor, that RNG seeding and literature citations are absent, and that the script's output file (turing_patterns_black_neon.gif, custom black-neon palette without axes) does not match docs/media/turing_gray_scott.gif. Overall 40.9/100 (faithfulness 43.4, reproducibility 35.0; model-implementation 57.0/100, biological-validation 33.1/100, applicable-only overall 37.8/100; uncalibrated rubric score, not a calibrated probability); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 5659d5e; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, pandas 2.3.3, scikit-image 0.26.0, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 68, Morphological realism / specimen match 50, Parameter expressivity 35, Morphometric validation 5, Source and data traceability 15, Code-to-model traceability 30, Reproducibility package 55. Output judged: turing_patterns.gif: rendered output of 1952-turing-morpho.py at 5659d5e, image/gif, 14075347 B, 1280×960 px, 500 frames, sha256 0ddf48cbca6cf3df80bf611fded797346cb34d93a3308897ed7d2f2005c20c84." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott> ;
    pk:hasProbability 4.09e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-turing-gray-scott-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Gray-Scott reaction-diffusion patterns — Parameter expressivity: 35/100" ;
